const explanations=['Six native process scenarios cover version/schema/identity/endpoints and cascading relink order; portable rollback/history contracts and process held-lock checks pass.','Held uncommitted native-plus-receipt commands reject identical and differing concurrent intents busy, then retain exact original success, reject conflicting committed intent and repeat known success without writes. Native/evaluation and HTTP identity races preserve one outcome.','Independent reader snapshot remains at revision1 while another process commits revision2; readers run under held writer; attempted read-only writes reject and next write succeeds. New evidence rejects old HTTP continuation; separate requests do not share snapshots.','Independent engineering/research activity-capture, result-selection, disposition/action and changed-basis tasks retain one guarded result and reject stale inputs/unsupported completion. Actual-project and research reopen races retain original evidence and exact configuration pair meaning.','Worker termination before commit restores complete prior export; after commit retains native/receipt/outcome for inspection. Two server processes, restarted server and CLI inspect a deliberately dropped committed response after exactly one POST.','SQLite online backup during held actual-project writes restores exact preceding committed export and controlled application reads. Original and complete restored outcome ledgers are separately compared before final publication.','Pre-change synthetic baseline; explicitly disclosed post-correctness-fix real baseline, fixed budgets before subsequent workload work and no query optimization. Actual and connected-synthetic 2/4 readers plus writer meet budgets; all56 dependency pages streamed, response cap rejected explicitly, query calls/payload/rows measured with stated limitations.','New independent HTTP/client and CLI proof plus unchanged full shared workspace, interface and recovery regressions. Different schema